<item>
            <title>[KYLIN-6050] Tables in the `default` Database Cannot Be Directly Queried When Only the Table Name Is Specified in the SQL Statement</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-6050</link>
                <project id="12316121" key="KYLIN">Kylin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When querying a table in the `default` database by specifying only the table name in the SQL statement, and directly querying an internal table, the system fails to prepend `INTERNAL_CATALOG` to the table name. As a result, the query targets Hive data instead of the intended internal table.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13609044">KYLIN-6050</key>
            <summary>Tables in the `default` Database Cannot Be Directly Queried When Only the Table Name Is Specified in the SQL Statement</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
