                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17928367" author="JIRAUSER298470" created="Wed, 19 Feb 2025 09:32:58 +0000"  >&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RootCause&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Root Cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the option to directly query internal tables is selected, `SchemaConverter` parses the table name from the SQL and prepends the internal table schema (`INTERNAL_CATALOG.{project}`) to the table name to enable direct querying of internal tables. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, `SchemaConverter` only recognizes table names in the `DB.TABLE` format. When the database name is omitted in the SQL, it fails to identify the table name. As a result, the internal table schema is not prepended, and the query defaults to using the Hive schema instead. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;DevDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Dev Design&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix `SchemaConverter` to correctly identify cases where the database name is omitted in the SQL. Specifically: &#160;&lt;br/&gt;
1. Ensure that the table name is recognized even when the database name is not explicitly specified. &#160;&lt;br/&gt;
2. Handle edge cases, such as distinguishing between table names and aliases defined in `WITH` clauses following the `FROM` clause. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
